// Windows resources for the ClipFlow executable.
//
// The icon is compiled into the .exe so Windows shows it in the taskbar, in
// the Start menu, in Explorer and in the Add/Remove Programs list. Without it
// the shipped binary shows the generic "unknown application" icon, and so does
// every shortcut the installer creates.
//
// This file lives next to `icon.ico` on purpose. The resource compiler is
// invoked from different working directories by the different toolchains
// (rc.exe resolves relative to the crate root, llvm-rc relative to this file's
// directory), so "icon.ico" next to this .rc is the only spelling that
// resolves under both. build.rs also passes `icons/` as an include directory.
1 ICON "icon.ico"
